   ],
   "rot": 150,
   "text": "VESPERGARD kept the Evening Vigil for nine hundred years.\n\nWake. Watch. Wait.\n\nThe door you came by is already forgotten. Only forward now, Latecomer \u2014 the Cloister remembers itself for you, a while longer."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    1.8,
    0,
    1.6
   ],
   "rot": -135,
   "text": "THE GARTH LANTERN\n\nKneel, and keep vigil.\n\nKnow this: the seeing ends when the vigil begins. What you have walked in memory you must then walk in truth, and the truth has teeth. While the quarter's warden grieves, the memory will not take again.\n\nPut him to rest. Then keep, or quench, as you please."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    -9.5,
    0,
    -13.6
   ],
   "rot": 130,
   "text": "CHAPTER HOUSE OF THE GRAY CLOISTER\n\nOn the last evening the sun went down and did not rise. The brothers rang the hours anyway. They lit six hundred candles and then six thousand, and when the wax ran out they gave their own.\n\nThe thirteenth hour never came. It is still not come. Mind you are not here when it does."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    0,
    0,
    -11.2
   ],
   "rot": 180,
   "text": "THE SISTERS' PLOT\n\nLet them keep what they carried.\n\n(The gate is rusted fast. Through the bars: quiet tombs, and a cold gleam of candleglass among the stones.)"
  }
